  "conclusions": [
    "Full board history corrects a confirmed train/eval input mismatch and substantially improves the one-epoch checkpoint, without changing weights.",
    "The corrected one-pass model still trails Hero1 on the original descriptive development opening set. No confirmation or search launch.",
    "Eight-pass refinement remains substantially worse than one pass; extra inference steps are not a strength improvement.",
    "The unchanged Hero1/raw current-only anchor reproduces its prior aggregate WDL and pentanomial exactly.",
    "Matched root-policy CE improves with correct history, but Hero1 and the corrected checkpoint have nearly the same top-1 accuracy; lower imitation loss is not evidence of stronger play."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "All raw-BT4 arena baselines deliberately remain current-only to isolate candidate input effects; this does not measure full-history raw LC0 or LC0 search strength.",
    "Opening ranges are reused development data, not a new held-out confirmation.",
    "Score intervals are marginal paired Hoeffding intervals, not matrix-wide simultaneous intervals.",
    "The matched policy losses are t=0/all-masked root CE, not the unlike original aggregate training objectives.",
    "Remaining strength differences cannot be uniquely attributed among the changed data, losses, optimizer precision, learning rates, decay, or training duration."
  ],
